<title>USA: Brite says gets Swedish phone contract.</title>
<headline>Brite says gets Swedish phone contract.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brite Voice Systems Inc said Sweden's Telia Mobitel AB chose Brite to provide voice activated dialing for Telia subscribers.</p>
<p>It said initial contract value is $2.3 million.</p>
<p>Brite customers can make mobile phone calls by speaking the name or telephone number of the person they wish to call.</p>
<p>Due for launch during 1997, Telia Mobitel will implement Brite's voice dialing on analog and digital networks.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
